 - CI: Pest test gate on PRs/push via `bin/pf shell` ([#21](https://github.com/PegaFila/PegaFilaWeb/pull/21)).
 - Queue management domain slice: `CreateQueue`/`UpdateQueue` (no delete — deactivation preserves tickets), `queue_access` grants (`QueuePermission::call` only), `SetQueueAccess` with audit trail, `QueuePolicy` as the centralized authorization source, and the same call rule enforced by both `CallNextTicket` and `Ticket::call`.
 - Editor/agent LSP support: Intelephense (general PHP) and first-party Laravel LSP (routes, views/Blade, config, Livewire) wired via `opencode.json`, shared `.claude/settings.json`, and `.vscode/` workspace settings ([#25](https://github.com/PegaFila/PegaFilaWeb/pull/25)).
+- Totem BFF API: Four stable endpoints for the Flutter client (`routes/api.php`) — `POST /api/totem/auth` (pairing code login with JWT), `GET /api/{entity}/queues` (list queues with visual specs), `GET /api/{entity}/{queue}/priorities` (list priority levels), `POST /api/{entity}/{queue}/ticket` (issue ticket with chosen priority). JWT carries scope (totem/entity/preset/queues); middleware validates every call server-side (token, totem active, preset active, queue in scope). Rate limiting: 10 req/min for auth, 30 req/min for other endpoints. CORS for `localhost:*` and `127.0.0.1:*` (dev). Pairing Artisan command `totem:pairing-code {preset}` generates 6-digit code, logs with audit trail. Ticket channel `totem` reuses `IssueTicket` action with server-selected code; JWT secret and TTL configurable via `TOTEM_JWT_SECRET` and `TOTEM_JWT_TTL`. HS256 JWT with `jti` claim for single-use token tracking.
 
